<<~ ahu slot=`#/about`>>

! Streams Plugin — by Saq Imtiaz

A vendor declaration: this carrier names an outside artifact this tree carries, so a reader learns its
provenance and its terms without opening it.

''Author'': [[Saq Imtiaz|https://github.com/saqimtiaz/streams]]
''License'': BSD-3-Clause
''Upstream'': `saqimtiaz/streams`
''TW5 plugin id'': `$:/plugins/sq/streams`

Streams gives TiddlyWiki a hierarchical tree-of-tiddlers surface: keyboard-driven entry, Tab to indent,
Enter for a new node, and every node standing as an ordinary tiddler.

!! A deferred offering — this tree carries no packed bytes

Streams is DEFERRED (operator ruling): no packed plugin for it sits anywhere in this tree, and
genesis's boot set carries nothing beyond the engine core, the grammar and the boot shadows. This
carrier is the record of the terms an eventual offering would carry, written before the packing — a
future `nexus-publish`-style act packs the upstream bytes, mints a signed offering naming this same
licence and provenance, and carries it as a recipe-selected plugin (never a boot-set member) exactly
as `offerings/highlight/` already does for the PoC.

!! Two vocabularies for one tree

Streams and this grammar each name a tree of records, and they name it differently:

| the tree's | Streams | this grammar |
|---|---|---|
| upward edge | `parent` | `$fragment-parent` |
| ordered children | `stream-list` | `$slot`, in body order |
| node marker | `stream-type` | the `<<~ ahu>>` block itself |

''The correspondence holds; the projection does not enact it.'' A carrier's fragments carry the
grammar's names alone, so a wiki wanting Streams navigation over them writes the second pair from the
first — the shape is already there, and only the vocabulary is missing.

!! Packing it, when the deferral lifts

```
git clone --depth=1 https://github.com/saqimtiaz/streams.git
```

Pack the clone into a signed `PluginOffering` under a new `packages/lararium-tw5/offerings/streams/`
(the shape `scripts/pack-highlight-offering.ts` already demonstrates), never back into
`packages/lararium-tw5/plugins/` — that directory holds only the fixed boot set genesis packs, and
Streams never joins it. State the packed version in `tw5-plugin-version` above. ''The declaration is
the record of the terms this tree holds'', so a version packed and not reflected here leaves the
record saying one thing and the offering carrying another.

